From 890417e80da877778398d0efa28392e816331ea2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jiaxing Hu <huhuvmb88@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 6 Jun 2026 14:17:25 +1200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] plat-rockchip: rk3576: add secure boot PTA support
 (RSA-2048)

Add CFG_RK_SECURE_BOOT support for RK3576 with the following OTP layout
(cross-referenced against Rockchip vendor U-Boot secure OTP driver):

  Status word : OTP_S word 0x8  (bytes [32, 33])
  RSA key hash: OTP_S words 0x184-0x187 (bytes [1552, 1567])
                SHA-256 of RSA-2048 public key, 4 x 32-bit words

RK3576 supports RSA-2048 only (no RSA-4096 status fuse).
CFG_RK_SECURE_BOOT_SIMULATION defaults to y; set it to n to actually
fuse the hash (irreversible, may brick the device).

Also fix rk_secure_boot.c to support variable RSA hash sizes:
- Remove static_assert(ROCKCHIP_OTP_RSA_HASH_SIZE == 8) hardcoded size
- Make HASH_STRING_SIZE dynamic (RSA_HASH_SIZE * 11 + 1)
- Make otp_to_string() accept an explicit count parameter
- Gate write_key_size() RSA-4096 path on
  #ifdef ROCKCHIP_OTP_SECURE_BOOT_STATUS_RSA4096 so platforms that
  only support RSA-2048 compile without the unreachable branch
- Fix write_hash(): return TEE_ERROR_GENERIC instead of TEE_SUCCESS
  when the readback verification fails
- Fix lockdown_device(): use assignment instead of OR when writing the
  enable status (avoids accidental RSA4096 fuse if status was dirtied)
- Use MIN() for memcpy sizes across hash structs of different sizes

Tested on Radxa Rock 4D (RK3576, 12 GiB LPDDR5) with simulation=y:
PTA registers correctly, xtest 113/1 (baseline unchanged).

Co-authored-by: the-gabe <105918853+the-gabe@users.noreply.github.com>
Signed-off-by: Jiaxing Hu <huhuvmb88@outlook.com>
